WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:04.200
Jenna: On this episode of
Travel Dares: Season US,

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.717
I'll be playing a different tune

00:00:05.717 --> 00:00:08.734
as I learn an iconic craft
in America's Music City.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.130
Last episode, I got a clue

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.937
for where I'd end up on this episode.

00:00:19.937 --> 00:00:22.360
"Time to build the Music in the City."

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:25.350
So now, I'm here at
Moxy Nashville Downtown,

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.920
the only hotel on Honky Tonk Row.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.130
Nashville is also known

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.790
as the songwriting capital of the world.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:32.760
And today, I get to try my hand

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.783
at the local craft of guitar making.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.040
I am so excited for this
guitar build workshop.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.800
As someone who loves music,

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.713
I can't wait to make a guitar.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.103
Hey, I'm Jenna.

00:00:46.103 --> 00:00:47.350
Josh: Hi Jenna, I'm Josh.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.190
Jenna: Hey, Josh.
Josh: Welcome to the workshop.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.170
Jenna: Thanks for having me.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.440
How long have you been doing this?

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.850
Josh: This is our ninth year here.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:55.100
Jenna: And what motivated
you to open this place?

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.090
Josh: Well, I moved to
Nashville and I make guitars,

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.070
and I know how exciting
it is to make guitars,

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.097
so I decided to teach
people how to build guitars.

00:01:02.097 --> 00:01:04.010
Jenna: How do the different
elements of the guitar

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:05.600
affect the final product?

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.420
The tone, in terms of the shape,

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.420
the material, all of that?

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.860
Josh: There's a whole bunch of
things that affect the sound,

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.150
the electronics affect the sound,

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:15.090
the wood affects the sound,

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.430
There's a whole bunch of things.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:17.620
It's just like cooking.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:19.078
If you add a little extra something

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:20.222
to your chocolate chip cookies,

00:01:20.222 --> 00:01:22.040
Jenna: Right
Josh: They're gonna taste different,

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.332
but they're still gonna be awesome.

00:01:23.332 --> 00:01:26.060
Jenna: So what do you think
makes this course so unique?

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.750
Josh: We do everything in one day.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.870
Nobody in the world can
build a guitar in one day,

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.040
but somehow we've been
able to condense everything

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.560
into six to eight hours.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.530
Jenna: I think I'm ready to
get started. I'm so excited.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.957
Josh: Let's make some sawdust.

00:01:38.957 --> 00:01:39.790
Jenna: Yes!

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:41.037
Josh: I got an apron for you.

00:01:41.037 --> 00:01:41.928
Jenna: Is that my name?

00:01:41.928 --> 00:01:42.761
Josh: That is your name.

00:01:42.761 --> 00:01:43.980
Jenna: I love this so much.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:45.620
Josh, I feel like this is the beginning

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:46.920
of a beautiful friendship.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:49.853
Josh: All right, Jenna.

00:01:49.853 --> 00:01:50.686
Ready to get started?

00:01:50.686 --> 00:01:51.519
Jenna: Yes!
Josh: All right.

00:01:51.519 --> 00:01:52.715
The first step that we're gonna do,

00:01:52.715 --> 00:01:53.910
is we're gonna sand the guitar bodies.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:54.743
Jenna: Okay.

00:01:54.743 --> 00:01:57.100
Josh: Now, we have to sand the
guitar body nice and smooth

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.420
so the wood is smooth

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.160
and will absorb the stain a lot better.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.080
So, we are going to sand
the front face first.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.910
We're gonna use the sander
for about two minutes on this.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:06.890
We're gonna flip it over,

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:09.203
and do the exact same
thing on the backside.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:13.727
(upbeat bluegrass music)

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:17.700
The next thing that we're going to do is,

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.570
we're gonna sand the edges.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.823
And you just go with
the grain a little bit,

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:24.180
until it's nice and smooth.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.173
Now that we're done here,

00:02:26.173 --> 00:02:27.760
do you wanna go over to the laser engraver

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:28.660
and add some flair?

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:29.800
Jenna: I love flair.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.468
Josh: Excellent, let's go then.

00:02:31.468 --> 00:02:32.690
Jenna: Okay.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.982
(upbeat bluegrass music)

00:02:39.654 --> 00:02:40.751
Josh: There it is.

00:02:40.751 --> 00:02:42.700
Jenna: That's awesome.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:43.700
Josh: All right, Jenna.
Jenna: Yes?

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.913
Josh: The next step is
staining the guitar body.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:49.780
This is the finish that you've chosen.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:53.140
This is a three-tone, faded sunburst.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.080
The recipe is on the back.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.520
We're gonna use three colors,

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.340
yellow, red, and a mahogany.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.880
Now, by the time you're done,

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.284
I guarantee it's gonna look good.

00:03:02.284 --> 00:03:04.551
(upbeat bluegrass music)

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.183
Jenna: What do you think?

00:03:11.183 --> 00:03:12.220
Josh: I think you did an amazing job.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:13.610
Jenna: Thank you.
Josh: Congratulations.

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:14.530
Jenna: I'm feeling really good about it.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:15.990
Josh: So are you ready to
go on to the next step?

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:16.890
Jenna: Mhmm.
Josh: Excellent.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.070
The first thing that we have to do

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:20.564
is we have to put the
tuners onto the guitar.

00:03:20.564 --> 00:03:21.397
Jenna: Okay.

00:03:21.397 --> 00:03:22.230
Josh: And after we've done that,

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.210
then we start assembling
all the other hardware

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.662
onto the guitar body.

00:03:25.662 --> 00:03:26.495
Jenna: OK.

00:03:26.495 --> 00:03:28.600
Josh: Once that's all
done, we put the neck on,

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.000
and then, soon after, we're
going to put strings on it

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:31.833
and play it.

00:03:31.833 --> 00:03:33.128
Let's get to it.

00:03:33.128 --> 00:03:35.711
(upbeat music)

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.350
You did it!

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.183
Jenna: The guitar's done.

00:03:57.183 --> 00:03:58.016
Josh: It's done.

00:03:58.016 --> 00:03:59.520
So now, we have to play it.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.510
Are you ready?

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:01.343
Jenna: Yes.

00:04:01.343 --> 00:04:02.630
Josh: Okay. Well come this way.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.550
I got a special guest for
you in the other room.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:05.870
Jenna: Oh, I can't wait to meet them.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:06.703
Josh: Excellent.

00:04:08.685 --> 00:04:10.768
(Max playing guitar)

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:18.590
Max: Oh, hey.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:19.490
Jenna: Ooo, hi.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.430
Josh: Jenna, this is Nashville
legend, Max T. Barnes.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:23.540
Max: Hey, how are ya?

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:24.942
Jenna: Hi!
Max: Nice to meet you.

00:04:24.942 --> 00:04:25.775
Jenna: It's so nice to meet you, yeah.

00:04:25.775 --> 00:04:27.020
Max: What'd y'all do today? Anything?

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.480
Jenna: Built a guitar, can you believe it?

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.320
Max: You built that?

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:31.580
Jenna: Yes. The whole
thing, start to finish.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:32.720
Max: Is that right?
Jenna: Yeah, it was incredible.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:33.733
Max: The color and everything?

00:04:33.733 --> 00:04:34.840
Jenna: Stained it at all.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.610
This one is an amazing teacher.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:37.470
Max: That's amazing.
Josh: Thank you.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:38.303
Max: Good job.
Jenna: Yeah.

00:04:38.303 --> 00:04:39.290
Max: It's a gorgeous guitar.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:40.732
Well, welcome to Nashville.

00:04:40.732 --> 00:04:41.565
Jenna: Thanks for having me.

00:04:41.565 --> 00:04:42.840
Max: They call it Music
City, do you know why?

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:43.950
Jenna: I have no idea.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.482
Max: Well, the lore goes,

00:04:45.482 --> 00:04:47.172
that there was an insurance company,

00:04:47.172 --> 00:04:48.722
in the mid last century,

00:04:48.722 --> 00:04:49.755
they had a little radio show

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:51.560
and they would have local people come in

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.270
and sing bluegrass and country music,

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.910
and they would broadcast that.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:57.320
And one thing led to another
and it got too big for that,

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.870
so they moved into this
neat, old church downtown,

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:01.450
built in the 1800s,

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.950
called the Ryman Auditorium,

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:05.090
and they still do concerts there now.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.231
And then they built the
Grand Ole Opry House.

00:05:07.231 --> 00:05:08.500
So that's how that all got started,

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.090
because the announcer
would call this Music City

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:12.330
and it stuck.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.810
Well, let's see how that thing works.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:14.910
Shall we plug it in and play together?

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.470
Jenna: Yes, I'm very
excited to see how it works.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:17.413
Max: There you go.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:20.243
Very good.

00:05:20.243 --> 00:05:21.510
All right, well,

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:23.380
have you played a lot of
electric guitar before?

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.462
Jenna: I've never played
an electric guitar before.

00:05:24.462 --> 00:05:26.379
Max: Have you not? Well, let
me show you a few things.

00:05:26.379 --> 00:05:28.310
A few tricks and tips, kid.
(Jenna laughs)

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.170
Here's how it goes.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.237
Well, the first thing you gotta know is,

00:05:31.237 --> 00:05:32.070
none of this matters,

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:33.471
it's pretty much just all,

00:05:33.471 --> 00:05:35.128
you gotta get that face on.

00:05:35.128 --> 00:05:36.739
Jenna: I knew it!

00:05:36.739 --> 00:05:38.641
Max: You gotta learn
that face right there.

00:05:38.641 --> 00:05:39.474
(guitars strumming)

00:05:39.474 --> 00:05:40.307
Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:05:40.307 --> 00:05:41.450
Jenna: Like that?
Max: That's pretty good.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:44.262
When you start playing a little bit,

00:05:44.262 --> 00:05:46.812
and get your shoulder into it.

00:05:46.812 --> 00:05:49.362
(Jenna and Max strumming the guitar)

00:06:05.383 --> 00:06:07.313
Max: Big, big ending, ready?
Jenna: Yeah

00:06:07.313 --> 00:06:10.996
Max: You go, (Max
strumming guitar quickly)

00:06:12.988 --> 00:06:15.390
Then you can take your
pick and go, "Woohoo!"

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:16.473
Jenna: Woohoo!

00:06:16.473 --> 00:06:18.480
Max: That's it, welcome to
Nashville, you graduated.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.370
Jenna: Yes! Thanks for having me.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:21.403
Max: Very good.

00:06:21.403 --> 00:06:22.953
(upbeat music)

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.200
My day at the Guitar Build Workshop

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.460
was such an incredible experience.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.870
I think my favorite part was
watching the assembly of it

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.150
and seeing it all come together,

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:38.240
it was just so satisfying.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.580
And I got to build my own custom guitar.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.300
I felt like a total rock star.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.550
When you come to Nashville,
do yourself a favor,

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:47.570
venture off Broadway and
give it a try yourself.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:49.040
Bartender: Here's your drink and clue.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.540
Jenna: I'll just close out, thanks.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.720
Oh, final clue.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.970
Let's see where we're
going on our last stop.

00:06:56.967 --> 00:07:00.400
"Check out these hoppy hot springs."

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.600
I dunno, are we gonna be jumping a lot?

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:05.960
I'm not sure, but I'm
very excited to find out.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:07.325
Until next time.

00:07:07.325 --> 00:07:08.567
(upbeat rock music)

